# API & webhooks (D-47)

Inspired by Lazy Developer Lock-It-Down + ECC secrets discipline (MIT patterns; DIAL-authored).

- Mutating / side-effect handlers need JWT, verified webhook signature, or fail-closed `INTERNAL_API_SECRET` (or mTLS).
- Never take `userId` / `email` / `role` from body or query — session/JWT only.
- After AuthN, call `assertResourceAccess` (or equiv) for object `:id` resources.
- `/webhooks/*` (Paynow, ContiPay, EcoCash, PayPal, Meta WA, FDMS): verify signature **and** idempotency key before mutate.
- Validate payloads with Zod at the boundary (forms, WA Flow data_exchange, PSP callbacks).
- Prefer audit report (`docs/agent-audits/endpoint-audit.md`) before drive-by fixes.
